  "title": "All Minimum Bondage Sets of an Eighteen-Vertex Counterexample",
  "batch_label": "66",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the fixed 18-vertex, 27-edge labelled graph G and lexicographic canonical convention frozen in source.md and problem.md, the family B_5(G)={F in binom(E(G),5): gamma(G-F)>gamma(G)=6} consists of exactly the 801 labelled five-edge sets serialized in evidence/bondage5_classification.json. Every such deletion has gamma(G-F)=7. Under the complete six-element group Aut(G), the family has exactly the 140 canonical orbits serialized in that file: 127 orbits have size 6 and setwise stabilizer order 1, and 13 have size 3 and setwise stabilizer order 2; each record gives the canonical representative and the complete stabilizer permutation list.",
